TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS: address layers, not runners
  pairwise observable=(shared predicates, predicate count, declaration order)
  switch/gauge=larger observable orients the edge
  scores={'birth_strip': 6, 'crossing_spine': 5, 'mirror_orbit': 4, 'gap_root': 3, 'endpoint_score': 2, 'cycle_packet': 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  tie Hamiltonian path=birth_strip > crossing_spine > mirror_orbit > gap_root > endpoint_score > cycle_packet > complement_even_dp

SYNTHESIS
  full recurrence clock: beta=a, with beta-layer size beta-2.
  half recurrence clock: tau=a+b-1, with crossing-layer size floor((tau-1)/2).
  combined address (beta,tau) recovers the tile and its one-flip root facts:
    b=tau-beta+1, gap=c3=2*beta-tau-2, H_oneflip=1+2^gap.
  dynamic payoff: n->n+1 adds n-1 full strip bits but only floor(n/2)
    new independent half-quotient orbit bits for complement-even invariants.
